# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, so anything not excluded here ships in the
# image. Two of these are correctness issues rather than size ones:
#
# `db.sqlite3` is the *developer's* database. It holds real account emails and
# password hashes, and without this line a local `make build` bakes them into a
# public image. CI never has one, which is exactly what makes the omission easy
# to miss.
#
# `.venv` is built for the host platform. Copying it into a linux/amd64 image
# shadows nothing at runtime but wastes hundreds of megabytes, and a stray
# `.pth` file in it can change import behaviour in ways that are baffling to
# debug.

.git
.github
.gitignore
.dockerignore

.venv
venv
env
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info
.pytest_cache

db.sqlite3
db.sqlite3-journal
.env
media
staticfiles

# Instance overlays name a specific community; the image is the product.
instances

# Docs and development-only assets. Nothing at runtime reads them.
docs
tests
helm
scripts
*.md
*.png
Makefile
pytest.ini
